-- title:
--   Admissible small constants, tame-fixed, at q = 2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, that is, the image of $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$. Then there exist an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in $A$ such that, writing $A_0$ for the pullback of $A$ along $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (so $A_0 = A \cap k_0$), the following hold: $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is the principal ideal generated by $\pi_0$; $A_0$ is a henselian local ring; the residue field of $A_0$ is algebraically closed; every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element $c$ of $k_0$ lying in $A$; $k_0$ is stable under every $\mathbb{Q}$-automorphism $\tau$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $x \in A \iff \tau x \in A$ for all $x$; and $k_0$ is fixed pointwise by the kernel of the tame character, in the sense that for every $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` (the image in the group of $\mathbb{Q}$-automorphisms of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$) with `A.tameCharacter π τ = 1`, i.e. with the residue of $\tau\pi/\pi$ in the residue field of $A$ equal to $1$, one has $\tau x = x$ for all $x \in k_0$. Moreover there exist a prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ together with a unit $u$ of $A$ such that $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\,u$.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ case of the construction of a field of "admissible small constants" inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$: a henselian discretely valued subfield with algebraically closed residue field carrying all the residues of $A$, stable under the decomposition group of $A$ and fixed by the kernel of the tame character, and containing a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity and a prescribed $(q^2-1)$-st root of $q$ up to a unit. It is used in the construction of supersingular prolongations and nodal charts on modular curves of full level in the case $q = 2$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ValuationSubring_exists_admissible_smallConstants_tameFixed_of_eq_two.lean

